+         CALL (with 'k' flag set) / JMP / OP_SETTOP. The OP_SETTOP (which
+         also fixes the stack top; see lvm.c) holds the number of nil
+         slots minus one in its B field: a positive 'nresults' needs
+         exactly that many nils; otherwise B stays 0 (a single nil). */
+      if (nresults > 0)  /* fixed positive number of results? */
+        SETARG_B(fs->f->code[pc + 2], nresults - 1);  /* widen OP_SETTOP */
